I replaced the 16‑bit index table with a table of precomputed `MESG*` pointers, so the hot path is a single load with no index arithmetic, multiply, or null-conditional; the pointer entries touched during decoding are few and stay in L1.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const MESG* index[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;
    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; ++i)
        {
            const FIT_UINT16 n = mesgs[i].num;
            if (index[n] == NULL)
                index[n] = &mesgs[i];
        }
        initialized = true;
    }
    return index[num];
}
```